          %h3#AlgebraicKTheory Algebraic K-theory
          %p
            With the identification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1 Mod \simeq FinSet^{\ast/}
            from
            %a{:href => "#Modules"} above
            it follows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+cohomotopy"} stable cohomotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
