                  K \mathbb{F}_1
                  \&amp; \coloneqq\;
                  K(\mathbb{F}_1 Mod)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq\;
                  K(FinSet)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  \\mathbb{S}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here in the first step we used the definition of algebraic K-theory for ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of the permutative category
            of modules (
            %a{:href => "K-theory+of+a+permutative+category#examples#OrdinaryAlgebraicKTheoryFromPermutativeCategoryOfProjectiveModules"}> this example
            ), in the second step we used the identification of modules over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Modules"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of the permutative category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} FinSet
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            (
            %a{:href => "K-theory+of+a+permutative+category#StableCohomotopyIsKTheoryOfFinSet"}> this example
            ), which is the spectrum representing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+cohomotopy"} stable cohomotopy
          %p
            The perspective that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathbb{F}_1
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            should be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Cohomotopy"} stable Cohomotopy
            has been highlighted in (
            %a{:href => "#Deitmar06"}> Deitmar 06, p. 2
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Guillot06"} Guillot 06
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Mahanta17"} Mahanta 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DundasGoodwillieMcCarthy13"} Dundas-Goodwillie-McCarthy 13, II 1.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MoravaSomeBackground"} Morava
            = succeed ").)," do
              %a{:href => "#ConnesConsani16"} Connes-Consani 16
            %a{:href => "#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10"} Chu, Lorscheid &amp; Santhanam 10, Thm. 5.9
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BeardsleyNakamura24"} Beardsley &amp; Nakamura 2024, Cor. 2.25
            %a{:href => "#ChuLorscheidSanthanam10"} Chu et al.
            also generalize to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+Cohomotopy"} equivariant stable Cohomotopy
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %p
            With the understanding of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
